A user device (200) comprising a display (206), an interface (208) for communication with a lamp comprising controllable light sources (104), and a processor (202) configured to execute an application (214), wherein the application is configured to:

control the lamp to emit light in accordance with a source light pattern (302), said source light pattern defining, for each light source, the light to be emitted by that light source and designating at least one of the light sources as a marker light source (308);

receive an image of the source light pattern as projected onto a target surface (300) by the lamp, wherein the image is captured by a camera (210), and wherein the target light pattern (310) within the image is distorted;

display the received image on the display;

detect the locations within the displayed image at which the marker light source or sources are positioned to emit, or intended to emit, light onto the target surface; and

utilise the detected locations of the marker light source or sources to align a control overlay over the displayed image, the control overlay identifying, for each light source, an area within the displayed image onto which the light source is intended to emit light, wherein the control overlay enables a user of the user device to control the light sources in response to at least one user selection.

