# Claim 1

**1.** A system for controlling a projector lamp, the system comprising:

a projector lamp having a plurality of individually addressable light sources configured to emit light forming a projected light pattern onto a surface; and

a mobile computing device having a camera, a display, and one or more processors configured to execute instructions that cause the mobile computing device to:

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;capture, via the camera, an image of the projected light pattern as projected onto the surface, wherein the projected light pattern is geometrically distorted relative to a physical arrangement of the plurality of individually addressable light sources due to at least one of a projection angle, a surface geometry, or a viewing perspective;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;determine a correspondence between one or more regions of the captured image of the distorted projected light pattern and respective ones of the plurality of individually addressable light sources;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;render, on the display, the captured image of the distorted projected light pattern together with a plurality of interactive control elements overlaid on the captured image, each interactive control element being spatially positioned in registration with a respective region of the distorted projected light pattern and associated with a corresponding one of the plurality of individually addressable light sources;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;receive, via a user interaction with a selected interactive control element, an input specifying an adjustment to an emission characteristic of the individually addressable light source associated with the selected interactive control element; and

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;transmit a control signal to the projector lamp to adjust the emission characteristic of the associated individually addressable light source in accordance with the received input, independently of the other individually addressable light sources.
